## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests understanding of partition dynamic programming with bitwise operations, commonly encountered in optimization scenarios for data processing and segmentation tasks.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP formulation
- Subarray OR precomputation
- Boundary reconstruction
- Time/space complexity analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxOrPartition(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const OR = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(n+1).fill(0));

  // Precompute OR for all subarrays
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    let cur = 0;
    for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
      cur |= A[j];
      OR[i][j+1] = cur;
    }
  }

  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
        if (dp[j][t-1] !== -Infinity) {
          const val = dp[j][t-1] + OR[j][i];
          if (val > dp[i][t]) {
            dp[i][t] = val;
            par[i][t] = j;
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct blocks
  const blocks = [];
  let curr = n;
  for (let t = k; t >= 1; t--) {
    const start = par[curr][t];
    blocks.unshift([start, curr-1]);
    curr = start;
  }

  return { maxSum: dp[n][k], blocks };
}
```

## Complexity
Time: O(n²k) due to triple nested loops, Space: O(nk + n²) for DP tables and OR precomputation.

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical tree DP approach: building a connected component of fixed size while propagating choices up a rooted tree, including reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Tree knapsack DP for connected subgraphs
- Subtree containment and topmost node principle
- Reconstruction via parent/child pointers
- Time/space: O(N*K^2) in naive merge, with optimizations possible

## Code Example
```javascript
function dfs(u, p) {
  dp[u] = new Array(size[u] + 1).fill(-Infinity);
  dp[u][1] = val[u];
  for (const v of g[u]) if (v !== p) {
    dfs(v, u);
    // merge dp[u] with bestChild from v
    const ndp = new Array(size[u] + size[v] + 1).fill(-Infinity);
    for (let a = 1; a <= size[u]; a++) {
      if (dp[u][a] === -Infinity) continue;
      // option: take nothing from v
      ndp[a] = Math.max(ndp[a], dp[u][a]);
      for (let b = 1; b <= size[v]; b++) {
        if (best[v][b] === -Infinity) continue;
        ndp[a + b] = Math.max(ndp[a + b], dp[u][a] + best[v][b]);
      }
    }
    size[u] += size[v];
    dp[u] = ndp;
  }
}
```

